        a                 ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment      "Silk cravat, England, ca. 1870"@en , "Cravat of lilac and gray figured silk with a design suggesting water marks and pine cones. It is made on the straight of the material, and has square ends and is shaped in at the back of the neck, where a machine embroidered label is stitched. Interlined with cotton-demette."@en ;
